content.text:
{
  "key": "pr-887",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "fix(ado): PR comments read cleanly on Azure DevOps",
    "description": "Fixes #881 and #882.\n\n**#881** — the review-verdict record's explanatory sentence named `gh-807` and the SM tick. The machine marker (what the SM actually parses) is identical for every provider; only the human sentence below it changes: neutral text for ADO/azure, unchanged for GitHub / no provider. Provider from `config.scm.provider`.\n\n**#882** — `Automated Rework Started` put a fenced block inside a bullet inside a blockquote; ADO shows a broken stack of ``` lines. Bullets and the log file names now use single-line code spans (`m.inline`) in `preCliReworkSetup` and `preparePRForReview` (same CI panel) and two inline sentences elsewhere. Standalone error blocks keep `m.code`. Jira wiki output is byte-identical.\n\nTests: 4 new; the 3 behavioural ones fail on the unfixed code. Suite 2612 passed. Not verified on a live ADO PR."
  }
}

