{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: GitLab verdict records keep the internal gh-807 wording + duplicated expression**

Two small points on this conditional:

1. **GitLab is not covered.** `config.scm.provider` also admits `'gitlab'` (`js/common/scm.js` `createScm`), and the GitLab provider's `addComment` posts verdict records to MRs. With this change a GitLab MR still shows *"Review verdict record (gh-807) — machine-parsed by the SM tick…"* — the same internal-jargon-on-a-foreign-UI issue `agents#881` fixes for ADO. The comment above says "other SCMs (Azure DevOps) get a neutral one", but the implementation neutralizes only `ado`/`azure`. If GitLab is deliberately out of scope, fine — but then say `'gitlab'` keeps the GitHub text explicitly; otherwise a one-word addition (`|| p === 'gitlab'`) closes the gap.

2. **Duplicated expression.** `String(provider || '').toLowerCase()` is evaluated twice in the same condition. Hoisting it reads cleaner:

```js
var p = String(provider || '').toLowerCase();
var note = (p === 'ado' || p === 'azure')
    ? '🤖 Automated review record. Please do not edit or reply.'
    : '🤖 Review verdict record (gh-807) — machine-parsed by the SM tick to ' +
      'reconcile contradictory review legs on one head. Do not edit or reply.';
```

